{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"adored-duskish-kissingbug","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\nTicket 699f replaced the per-test store build in `tests/interfaces/conftest.py` with a per-worker template that each test copies. Its acceptance criterion read: \"The template fixture asserts it is virgin (no tickets, no `<repo>/.rebar/`).\"\n\nThe landed change (Gerrit 1063, merged) satisfies only HALF of that. `_rebar_repo_template` asserts `not (repo / \".rebar\").exists()` but never asserts the template carries no tickets. The no-tickets half is checked only by a separate test, `tests/interfaces/test_rebar_repo_isolation.py::test_template_stays_virgin`. The completion verifier caught this and correctly refused to close 699f.\n\nWhy this matters rather than being a wording nit: the invariant is that the template must NEVER be pre-seeded. Several tests in the tier assert on emptiness (session-log counts in `tests/interfaces/queries/test_recent_session_logs.py` and `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_session_log_capture.py`) and hold only because nothing seeds the template. The obvious next optimisation -- pre-warming the template with tickets so tests skip setup -- would silently invert those assertions.\n\nA fixture-level assertion fails at CONSTRUCTION, once per worker, before any test runs, and covers every consumer. A test-level assertion fires only when that one test is selected, so a narrowed run such as `pytest tests/interfaces/store` has no protection at all. Closing that gap is the reason to fix this properly rather than argue the criterion into compliance.\n\n## Approach\nAdd the missing assertion to `_rebar_repo_template` in `tests/interfaces/conftest.py`, immediately after `rebar.init_repo()` and the root commit, INSIDE the existing `pytest.MonkeyPatch.context()` block. It must sit inside that block because the assertion needs `REBAR_ROOT` and cwd pinned at the template; the context exits before the current post-build assertions run, which is why the existing `.rebar` check is a plain filesystem test.\n\nKeep the existing `.rebar` assertion where it is: it needs no environment and reads more clearly beside the other post-build checks.\n\nRejected alternative: leave the check in `test_template_stays_virgin` only and record evidence on 699f to satisfy the verifier. The criterion would then read as met while the narrowed-run gap above stays open. That is gaming the gate, not meeting it.\n\nRejected alternative: assert at the filesystem level (no ticket directories under `.tickets-tracker`) to avoid needing the pinned environment. That works, but it duplicates knowledge of the store layout that `rebar.list_tickets()` already owns, and would miss a ticket recorded anywhere the layout check does not look.\n\n## Scope\n- `tests/interfaces/conftest.py` -- one assertion inside the template fixture's MonkeyPatch context.\n\n`test_template_stays_virgin` STAYS. It is not made redundant: it also asserts `.rebar` absence from a test context and documents the invariant where a reader of the sentinel file will look for it. This ticket adds enforcement at construction; it does not move the existing check.\n\n## Testing\nNo new behavior -- this adds an assertion to existing test infrastructure, so no new test is warranted.\n\nThe assertion must be shown to be load-bearing rather than decorative: seed a ticket into the template right after the build, confirm the fixture raises, then remove the seed and confirm the tier passes. That is a temporary local check; the durable evidence is the tier passing with the assertion in place.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `_rebar_repo_template` in `tests/interfaces/conftest.py` asserts the freshly built template has no tickets, inside the MonkeyPatch context where REBAR_ROOT and cwd are pinned.\n- [ ] The existing `.rebar` absence assertion is retained.\n- [ ] `tests/interfaces/test_rebar_repo_isolation.py::test_template_stays_virgin` is retained and passes.\n- [ ] `python -m pytest tests/interfaces -q` passes with the same collected/passed counts as before this change.\n- [ ] `make lint` passes.\n- [ ] `make typecheck` passes.","id":"446c-1d56-9163-499d","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Assert template has no tickets inside the fixture, not only in a test"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785454159589506001,"uuid":"6d8a0e8c-744c-434b-9267-65398ba5a47a"}